{
  "title": "AST/ALT ratio does not demonstrate incremental cognitive-score prediction across two NHANES samples",
  "abstract": "In 1,287 NHANES 2011\u20132012 adults aged 60+ and 1,505 separately sampled 2013\u20132014 adults, AST/ALT ratio added to flexible separate enzymes and clinical/demographic predictors did not demonstrate improved concurrent DSST prediction: target weighted MSE difference +0.129069 (+0.0757%), with source-refit/target PSU-bootstrap 95% interval [-0.473677, 1.804713] score-squared units. This is not evidence of equivalence or absence of an enzyme\u2013cognition association.",
